  "intro": "<p>Star names are easy to find in almost every language: Stella in Latin, Seren in Welsh, Tara in Sanskrit, Sitara in Urdu, Najm in Arabic, Yıldız in Turkish, Hoshi in Japanese. This list collects real given names whose meaning is 'star', 'morning star' or a named star, each checked against a cited source, mostly Behind the Name and Wiktionary. Ranks for England and Wales, where they exist, come from the ONS.</p><p>A few famous 'star' names aren't what they seem. Esther may or may not mean 'star'; Astrid doesn't; and Mary's 'star of the sea' is a title, not a meaning. We've marked these uncertain and said why.</p>",
